&lt;p&gt;
	Following our food hygiene inspection On 27 October 2026, immediate corrective action was taken to address the matters identified.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	We have strengthened our food preparation and cross-contamination controls, updated relevant risk assessments and reinforced food safety procedures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	Additional staff training and supervisory checks have been introduced, with further comprehensive face-to-face food safety training being arranged through our external food safety consultants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	We take our food safety responsibilities extremely seriously and remain fully committed to ensuring these improvements are maintained consistently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	Aviator Hotel has consistently maintained a Food Hygiene Rating of 5 for many consecutive years, supported by established food safety procedures, regular staff training and management controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	The circumstances identified during the inspection were not representative Of our usual standards and we fully acknowledge that this was unacceptable. Immediate action was taken to rectify the issues identified.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	We recognise our responsibility for ensuring food safety procedures are followed at all times and have taken steps to prevent a recurrence.&lt;/p&gt;
